//- Account created
//-
//- Rendered with the serialized User as the model ( `_user_email` in actions.ts passes
//- `user.toJSON()` ), so only User fields are in scope: Login, Email, Uuid, CreatedAt,
//- RegisteredAt, LastLoginAt, IsActive. No absolute URL is available here — the deploying
//- application owns its own domain, so action links are left to a project override of this
//- template rather than guessed at.
doctype html
html
  head
    meta(charset='utf-8')
    title Account created
  body
    p Hello #{ Login || Email },
    p An account has been created for you.
    p
      | Sign in with: 
      strong #{ Email }
    p —
    p This is an automated message; please do not reply.
